8,PDF Indian Knowledge System in Practice: The Folk Traditions of the Sonowal ...,https://www.ijfmr.com/papers/2025/4/52888.pdf,"This research article aims to study the folk traditions of the Sonowal Kachari tribe as a part of the Indian Knowledge System. By focusing on their ritual practices, folk music and dance etc, the study seeks to highlight how indigenous knowledge I not only preserved but also practiced and adapted in contemporary settings.",Kachari,Sino-Tibetan
9,PDF The Cultural History of the Bodo Community: A Descriptive Study,https://www.ijfmr.com/papers/2025/5/55642.pdf,"The Bodo community, one of the earliest settlers in Assam, belongs to the Tibeto-Burman branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family. Historically referred to as the Bodo-Kachari, they are considered autochthons of the Brahmaputra Valley, with a presence dating back to the second millennium B.C..",Kachari,Sino-Tibetan
